      <div class="results-prose fade-in" id="ranking-method">
        <h2>How teams were ranked</h2>
        <p>Few submissions scored above zero on real hardware. Teams with a score above zero are ranked by score. To rank the remaining teams, the organizing committee assessed how far each policy progressed during the official evaluations:</p>
        <ul class="criteria">
          <li class="crit-t2"><span class="criteria-seq" aria-hidden="true"><span class="c-ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="5" y="2.5" width="14" height="3.5" rx="1.2"/><path d="M7.5 6v5.5L10 16M16.5 6v5.5L14 16"/><rect x="10" y="17" width="4" height="4" rx="1"/></svg></span><svg class="c-then" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3.5L10.5 8 6 12.5"/></svg><span class="c-ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="5.5" cy="18.5" r="2"/><circle cx="18.5" cy="5.5" r="2"/><path d="M7.5 18.5H15a3.25 3.25 0 0 0 0-6.5H9a3.25 3.25 0 0 1 0-6.5h7.5"/></svg></span></span>Task 2: grasp engagement first (whether the arm reached for the target and the gripper closed), then navigation.</li>
          <li class="crit-t3"><span class="criteria-seq" aria-hidden="true"><span class="c-ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="5.5" cy="18.5" r="2"/><circle cx="18.5" cy="5.5" r="2"/><path d="M7.5 18.5H15a3.25 3.25 0 0 0 0-6.5H9a3.25 3.25 0 0 1 0-6.5h7.5"/></svg></span><svg class="c-then" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3.5L10.5 8 6 12.5"/></svg><span class="c-ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="5" y="2.5" width="14" height="3.5" rx="1.2"/><path d="M7.5 6v5.5L10 16M16.5 6v5.5L14 16"/><rect x="10" y="17" width="4" height="4" rx="1"/></svg></span></span>Task 3: navigation first (how far the robot navigated toward the table), then arm engagement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Teams that could not be separated share a rank, and the next rank is skipped. The committee adopted this criterion after evaluation because the published criteria did not separate teams that scored zero. It applies only to those teams.</p>
